# CKli convention: every text file is UTF-8 WITHOUT a BOM and uses CRLF line endings.
#
# "text=auto eol=crlf" makes git store LF in the repository and check out CRLF in the working
# tree on every platform, so the convention no longer depends on each developer's core.autocrlf
# setting. Without it, a clone with core.autocrlf=false or input (Linux, most CI images) yields
# LF working files, which silently changes the value of every multi-line C# raw string literal
# and every golden-master test comparison that comes with it.
#
# Git cannot express the "no BOM" half of the convention: that one stays a review rule.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Binary content: never convert, never diff.
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.nupkg binary
*.ico binary
*.snk binary
